---
title: "Sequence 3 - Event Coordinator Lead reassigns an event (SCRUM-23, Week 7 Change #5)"
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Lead as Event Coordinator Lead
    participant API as lead.py + assignment.py<br/>POST /events/{id}/reassign
    participant N as notifications.py
    participant DB as Database
    actor Prev as Previous Coordinator
    actor NewC as New Coordinator
    actor Org as Organiser

    Lead->>API: reassign(coordinator_id)
    API->>API: body must have coordinator_id (else 422)
    API->>API: role must be lead (else 403, checked before the event is loaded)
    API->>DB: load Event (else 404)
    alt not Submitted / Under Review / Returned (SCRUM-85: Approved is refused too)
        API-->>Lead: 400
    end
    API->>DB: load target user
    alt not an active coordinator, no Coordinator yet, or same as current
        API-->>Lead: 400
    end

    API->>N: notify_former_coordinator(previous)
    Note right of N: sent BEFORE the change, while still entitled,<br/>stored without an event link
    N->>DB: add Notification "reassigned_away" -> Previous

    API->>DB: event.assigned_coordinator_id = new (exactly one)
    API->>DB: add CoordinatorReassignment (from, to, by, when)
    API->>DB: add CoordinatorAssignmentHistory (keeps round-robin fair)

    API->>N: notify(new coordinator) / notify(organiser)
    N->>DB: add "reassigned_to_you" -> New
    N->>DB: add "coordinator_changed" -> Organiser (names New)

    API->>DB: commit (all or nothing)
    API-->>Lead: 200 {event row, previous, reassigned_by}

    Note over Prev,NewC: status_rules.py checks the ASSIGNED coordinator,<br/>so from now on the previous one gets 403 and the new one can act
    DB-->>Prev: GET /notifications shows removal notice
    DB-->>NewC: GET /notifications shows new event
    DB-->>Org: GET /notifications shows new coordinator
